🚀 Data Analyst Roadmap – Your Step-by-Step Guide

🛠 Phase 1: Foundations of Data Analysis (2-3 Months)

Goal: Build a strong foundation in probability, statistics, and problem-solving.

1️⃣ Probability & Statistics

✅ Course: "Probability & Statistics MOOC" (6 weeks)✅ Book (Optional): Introduction to Probability (for deeper understanding)✅ Practice: Solve problems from the course & Khan Academy exercises.

2️⃣ Python Programming & Problem-Solving

✅ Course: Python for Applied Data Science (Coursera)✅ Practice: LeetCode, CodeSignal, HackerRank📌 Key Skills: Loops, functions, lists, dictionaries, file handling.

📊 Phase 2: Data Structures & Tools (2-3 Months)

Goal: Master data manipulation, visualization, and databases for real-world analysis.

3️⃣ Data Structures & Algorithms (DSA)

✅ Course: Data Structures & Algorithms (Coursera)✅ Practice: Focus on sorting, searching, hash maps, recursion.

4️⃣ Data Analysis & Visualization Tools

✅ Excel: YouTube Playlist✅ Power BI: YouTube Playlist✅ Tableau: YouTube Playlist📌 Project Idea: Create a sales dashboard using Power BI/Tableau.

💾 Phase 3: Databases & Data Handling (1-2 Months)

Goal: Learn SQL & NoSQL for structured and unstructured data storage.

5️⃣ Databases (SQL & MongoDB)

✅ SQL (Structured Data): YouTube Playlist✅ MongoDB (Unstructured Data): YouTube Playlist📌 Project Idea: Design an HR employee database & analyze sales trends with SQL.

📈 Phase 4: Real-World Projects & Business Applications (2-3 Months)

Goal: Apply all skills to real-world datasets and build a portfolio.

6️⃣ Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) & Storytelling

✅ Book: Practical Statistics for Data Scientists✅ Book: Storytelling with Data: Let’s Practice✅ Practice: Data cleaning & visualization with Pandas & Matplotlib.📌 Project Ideas:

Analyze COVID-19 trends using Python.

Build an interactive Power BI dashboard.

Perform customer segmentation using Python & SQL.

🎯 Phase 5: Portfolio Building & Job Applications

Goal: Build a strong portfolio and apply for data analyst jobs.

7️⃣ Showcase Your Portfolio

✅ Push projects to GitHub (with README files).✅ Write data analysis case studies on LinkedIn or Medium.✅ Participate in Kaggle competitions.📌 Apply for roles:

Data Analyst

Business Intelligence Analyst

Entry-Level Data Scientist

📌 What’s Next? (Optional Advanced Topics)

🔥 Machine Learning Basics (If interested in Data Science)🔥 Big Data (Spark, Hadoop, AWS Redshift, BigQuery)🔥 Advanced SQL & Data Engineering

📌 Summary: Your Data Analyst Learning Path

1️⃣ Probability & Statistics (MOOC + Optional Book)2️⃣ Python & Problem Solving (Coursera + Coding Platforms)3️⃣ Data Structures & Algorithms (Coursera + LeetCode)4️⃣ Data Tools (Excel, Power BI, Tableau)5️⃣ Databases (SQL & MongoDB)6️⃣ EDA & Storytelling (Books + Hands-on Projects)7️⃣ Portfolio Building & Job Applications

📌 Estimated Time: 8-12 months (depending on pace & dedication)📌 Hands-on projects at every step to reinforce learning.

